! ja_ax1a "IBOX-1", routine IBIN1-IBIN27, pp.24-25 (octal 004023.00-
! 004052.40): "BRANCH ON I BOX INDICATORS %B-IND%", all four groups --
! XF, XCZ, XVLZ and XVZ.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  index_result_indicators.strap pins the index RESULT
! indicators for the immediate operations, but every index word in it
! has flag 0, so XF -- the index flag indicator -- was pinned nowhere.
! This is the deck's own test of it, and being a transcription it meets
! the stronger of the two standards used in this suite.
!
! IT ALSO PINS THE BRANCH-AND-ZERO CLEAR.  The mnemonics here are the
! full grammar: a leading Z means BRANCH IF THE BIT IS OFF, a trailing
! Z means TURN THE BIT OFF after testing.  The listing's own comments
! give the truth table, and the block walks XF through both polarities
! and then clears it:
!
!   IBIN1  BZXF,$      hang up if bit off      XF on  -> no branch
!   IBIN2  BXF,$+1.0   dont branch if bit off  XF on  -> branch, over
!                                              a BD,$ "hang up if no branch"
!   IBIN3  BZXFZ,$     hang up if bit off OR TURN OFF -- no branch, and
!                                              the trailing Z clears XF
!   IBIN4  BXF,$       hang up if bit on       XF now off -> no branch
!   IBIN5  BZXF,$+1.0  branch if bit off       XF off -> branch, over
!                                              a BD,$ "hang up if bit on"
!
! So a model that never set XF hangs at IBIN1, and one that set it but
! ignored the trailing-Z clear hangs at IBIN4.  Both measured below.
!
! WHAT THIS ROUTINE DOES NOT PIN, measured rather than guessed.  Every
! group checks its indicator ON, and the only OFF it checks is the one
! the trailing-Z CLEAR produces -- never an indicator off because its
! condition is false.  So a model that sets XF, XCZ, XVLZ and XVZ
! unconditionally to 1 on every index load passes this entire routine.
! That was injected and it passed, which is the honest statement of the
! block's reach: it pins that each indicator can be turned on by the
! right load and turned off by the trailing Z, and nothing whatever
! about the conditions being discriminating.
!
! NOTHING ELSE IN THE SUITE CLOSES THAT HOLE either, so it is recorded
! as a hole rather than pointed at some other program.  I first wrote
! here that index_result_indicators.strap and the KV/KC programs were
! the complementary evidence.  They are not.  Every check in
! index_result_indicators is Z,$IND then the operation then a branch-
! IF-ON, so the same unconditional injection passes it too -- measured,
! not assumed.  The compares are a weaker disclaimer than I first
! wrote: they run through setIndexCmpIndicatorsF, which the injection
! above does not touch, and which DOES set XF from the flag.  So the
! compare path's XF is simply not covered either way by anything here.
! The block that would close it is a restart section on p.25
! -- there is one right after IBIN20 and another after IBIN27 -- if one
! of them reloads $X1 and then takes a BZ<ind> branch.
!
! THE SEED IS ONE WORD.  IBXWZO is value -1, flag 1, count 0, refill 0
! -- negative, flagged and zero-count at once, which is why the listing
! calls it "COMMON XW FOR XF,XCZ,XVLZ" and reuses it for the XCZ and
! XVLZ groups that follow (not transcribed here).
!
! A DISCREPANCY IN XW's FOURTH FIELD, recorded because it is unresolved
! rather than because it matters here.  It is narrower than it first
! looked, so what follows is the narrowed version.
!
! THE TWO TAPES AGREE ON THE THREE-OPERAND FORM: XW, value, count,
! refill.  Three rows say so, and every field of all three reconciles.
! On this same page, IBG88 XW,IBG80.04,IBG91,IBG82 assembles
! "4006.04 00 100420.10 08" -- value = the BIT address of IBG80.04,
! count = 04021 = IBG91's WORD, refill = 04010 = IBG82's word -- and
! IBG87 XW,IBG81.04,2,IBG88 gives count = 2, refill = 04016 = IBG88.
! On jb_ax4b p.67, I38K1 XW,0,0,I38XW3 assembles "0.00 00 000000.13 7C",
! refill = 05574 = I38XW3's word.  Same order on both tapes.
!
! THEY DIFFER ONLY IN THE FOUR-OPERAND FORM, and there is exactly one
! sample of it per tape.  Here IBXWZO XW,-1,0,0,4 assembles
! "0.01 C0 000000.00 00": the 4 lands as the FLAG, IBM bit 25, and
! refill stays 0.  On jb_ax4b, XW,0,0,0,%8=10000 assembles
! "0.00 00 000000.20 00": the last operand lands in the REFILL field,
! setting IBM bit 51, which is exactly where an 18-bit refill holding
! 2**12 puts it.  (That row is one line of a BIT_n table, so its
! neighbours walk the bit across the field and confirm the placement.)
! Both rows were read at 400 dpi.  No single field order satisfies both,
! and no single FIELD does either: a field left-justified at bit 25
! explains the 4 but not the 010000, and one right-justified at bit 63
! explains the 010000 but not the 4.
!
! Note that the deck's own control flow independently requires flag = 1
! here, whatever the printed byte says -- IBIN1 is BZXF,$ , "hang up if
! bit off", so XF must be ON after the LX.  The reading is not resting
! on the C0 alone.
!
! So: two XW conventions, plausibly two STRAP versions, since these are
! different programs.  C22-6531 and C28-6129 have no text layer to
! settle it.  What would settle it is a four-operand XW with a LARGE
! last field somewhere on ja_ax1a, or a small one on jb_ax4b -- either
! fixes the field width on its own tape.  This assembler treats the
! fourth field as a one-bit flag, so the source below writes 1 where the
! listing writes 4; the ASSEMBLED WORD is identical to the listing's,
! which is what the verify script checks.
!
! That deviation is load-bearing, not cosmetic.  If someone later
! "reconciles" it toward the jb_ax4b reading, XW,-1,0,0,1 becomes
! refill = 1 with flag = 0, XF never lights, and this block halts at
! IBIN1 -- which is precisely the first injection below.

        SLC, (8)4023.0
!
! ---- XF: the index flag ------------------------------------------
IBINX   LX, $X1, IBXWZO                      ! turn on XF, XCZ, XVLZ
IBIN1   BZXF, $                              ! hang up if bit off
IBIN2   BXF, $+1.0                           ! dont branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if no branch
IBIN3   BZXFZ, $                             ! hang up if bit off or turn off
IBIN4   BXF, $                               ! hang up if bit on
IBIN5   BZXF, $+1.0                          ! branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if bit on
        B, IBIN6                             ! branch out
IBXWZO  XW, -1, 0, 0, 1                      ! listing writes "XW,-1,0,0,4"
IBIN6   VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
!
! ---- XCZ: the index count zero -----------------------------------
! No reload: the XF group left the same index word in $X1, and its
! count is still zero.  The four groups share two constants between
! them, which is the whole reason the listing calls IBXWZO "COMMON".
IBIN8   BZXCZ, $                             ! hang up if bit off
IBIN9   BXCZ, $+1.0                          ! dont branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if no branch
IBIN10  BZXCZZ, $                            ! hang up if bit off or turn off
IBIN11  BXCZ, $                              ! hang up if bit on
IBIN12  BZXCZ, $+1.0                         ! branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if bit on
        B, IBIN13                            ! branch out
IBIN13  VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
!
! ---- XVLZ: the index value less than zero ------------------------
IBIN15  BZXVLZ, $                            ! hang up if bit off
IBIN16  BXVLZ, $+1.0                         ! dont branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if no branch
IBIN17  BZXVLZZ, $                           ! hang up if bit off or turn off
IBIN18  BXVLZ, $                             ! hang up if bit on
IBIN19  BZXVLZ, $+1.0                        ! branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if bit on
        B, IBIN20                            ! branch out
IBIN20  VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
!
! ---- XVZ: the index value zero -----------------------------------
! This group needs the OTHER constant: IBXWZO's value is -1, so XVZ is
! off under it, and the deck reloads $X1 with IBXWZ1 -- value 0, count
! 1, flag 0 -- to turn XVZ on.  A model that never sets XVZ hangs at
! IBIN22, measured.
!
! I first wrote here that a model computing XVZ as "not XVGZ" would
! pass the first three groups and fail in this one.  That is FALSE, and
! the injection that was supposed to confirm it passed instead.  XVZ is
! only ever observed under IBXWZ1, whose value IS zero, and there "not
! XVGZ" and "value is zero" agree.  The deck never observes XVZ under a
! nonzero value, so nothing here can tell the two rules apart.
IBIN21  LX, $X1, IBXWZ1                      ! turn on XVZ
IBIN22  BZXVZ, $                             ! hang up if bit off
IBIN23  BXVZ, $+1.0                          ! dont branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if no branch
IBIN24  BZXVZZ, $                            ! hang up if bit off or turn off
IBIN25  BXVZ, $                              ! hang up if bit on
IBIN26  BZXVZ, $+1.0                         ! branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if bit on
        B, IBIN27                            ! branch out
IBXWZ1  XW, 0, 1, 0, 0                       ! common XW for XVZ
IBIN27  VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
PASS    BEW, $
        END, IBINX
